    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116089" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠκεαν-ῖτις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>daughter of Ocean,</i> Virg.<i><span class="en">
				<u>G.</u>
				4.341
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj.
			<i>of, in, from the Ocean,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θούλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					4.3b
				</span></i>
			.<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠ. θάλασσα,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠκεανός</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ὠκ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>) the <i>shore of Ocean,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.2.28
			</span></i>.</div>
